          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %strong core
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            consists of those
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elements"} elements
            for which
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
            out of that ring have no choice as to how to act: that is, those
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \in R
            such that for any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g \colon R \to S
            we must have
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(r) = g(r)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
            these are precisely the elements on which the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coprojections"} coprojections
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                  %mo ⊔
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_1, i_2 \colon R \to R \sqcup R
            are equal. Since the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
            of commutative rings is their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            (see
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "category+of+monoids#PushoutOfCommutativeMonoids"} here
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi r
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi R
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi ℤ
                  %mi R
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  r \otimes 1
                  \\;=\;
                  1 \otimes r
                  \\;\; \in \; R \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}} R
                  \\,.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#core_of_a_ring Core of a ring
          %p
          #CoreOfARing.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              %strong (core of a ring)
              %br/
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unital+ring"} unital
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core+of+a+ring"} core
              is the following
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} sub-ring
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+abelian+groups"} tensor product of abelian groups
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mrow
                            %mi ℤ
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \otimes_{{}_{\mathbb{Z}}} R
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mi R
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} {
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi r
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo |
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi r
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi r
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mn 1
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi R
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mrow
                            %mi ℤ
                      %mi R
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    c R
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\Big\{
                    \\,
                    r \in R
                    \\,\left\vert\,
                    1 \otimes r \,=\, r \otimes 1
                    \\;\in\; R \otimes_{{}_{\mathbb{Z}}} R
                    \\right.
                    \\,
                    \\Big\}
            %p
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#BousfieldKan72"}> Bousfield &amp; Kan 1972, Sec. 1
            )
          %p
          #CoreAsEqualizerAndAsRegularImage.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (core as
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equalizer"} equalizer
                and as
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+image"} regular image
              %br/
              In
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category-theoretic
              terminology, Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CoreOfARing"}
              describes the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equalizer"} equalizer
              (
              %a{:href => "#Bousfield79"}> Bousfield 1979, 6.4
              )
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mi R
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi equ
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi R
                    %mover
                      %mo ⇉
                      %mphantom
                        %mi AAAAAA
                    %mi R
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mrow
                          %mi ℤ
                    %mi R
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    c R
                    \\xrightarrow{\;equ\;}
                    R
                    \\overset{\phantom{AAAAAA}}\rightrightarrows
                    R \otimes_{{}_{\mathbb{Z}}} R
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the top
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi R
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi e
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi id
                    %mi R
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    R
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\mathbb{Z} \otimes R
                    \\xrightarrow{e \otimes id}
                    R \otimes R
            %p and the bottom one is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi R
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi id
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi e
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi R
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi R
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    R
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    R \otimes \mathbb{Z}
                    \\xrightarrow{\;id \otimes e\;}
                    R \otimes R
                    \\,,
            %p with
            #eq:UniqueRingHomomorphismFromTheIntegers.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℤ
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mi e
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbb{Z}
                    \&amp;\xrightarrow{ \;e\; } &amp;
                    R
                    \\\
                    1 &amp;\mapsto&amp; 1
                    }
            %p
              denoting the unique
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+homomorphism"} ring homomorphism
              form the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CommutativeRings"} CommutativeRings
            %p
              Observing (by
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "CRing#CoproductIsTensorProduct"} this Prop.
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+abelian+groups"} tensor product of abelian groups
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mrow
                          %mi ℤ
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \otimes_{{}_{\mathbb{Z}}} R
              equipped with its canonically induced
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+structure"} structure
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CommutativeRings"} CommutativeRings
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mrow
                          %mi ℤ
                    %mi R
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi R
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    R \otimes_{{}_{\mathbb{Z}}} R
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    R \sqcup R
            %p
              this means equivalently that the core is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equalizer"} equalizer
              of the two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coprojections"} coprojections
              into the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mi R
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi equ
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi R
                    %mover
                      %mo ⇉
                      %mphantom
                        %mi AAAAAA
                    %mi R
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mi R
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi R
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi ℤ
                    %mi R
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    c R
                    \\xrightarrow{\;equ\;}
                    R
                    \\overset{\phantom{AAAAAA}}\rightrightarrows
                    R \sqcup R
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    R \underset{\mathbb{Z}}{\coprod} R
                    \\,,
            %p
              hence – since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CommutativeRings"} CommutativeRings
              – into the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofiber+coproduct"} cofiber coproduct
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi e
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} \xrightarrow{e} R
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:UniqueRingHomomorphismFromTheIntegers"} (1)
              with itself.
            %p
              In this form, the core is manifestly (
              %a{:href => "image#AsEqualizer"}> here
              ) the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+image"} regular image
              of the initial morphism
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi e
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} \xrightarrow{e} R
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mi R
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Im
                      %mi reg
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi e
                      %mi R
                      %mo )
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mphantom
                        %mi AA
                    %mi R
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    c R
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    Im_{reg}
                    \\left(
                    \\mathbb{Z} \xrightarrow{e} R
                    \\right)
                    \\xhookrightarrow{\phantom{AA}}
                    R
                    \\,,
            %p
              hence the smallest
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+monomorphism"} regular monomorphism
              into
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CommutativeRings"} CommutativeRings
          %p
          #DualInterpretation.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (geometric interpretation)
              %br/
              By
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+algebra+and+geometry"} duality between algebra and geometry
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi CommutativeRings
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CommutativeRings^{op}
              as that of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+scheme"} affine
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+schemes"} arithmetic schemes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi CRing
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \in CRing
              we write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(R)
              for the same object, but regarded in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi CRing
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing^{op}
            %p
              So the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CRing"} CRing
              becomes the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spec%28Z%29"} Spec(Z)
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi CRing
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing^{op}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              there is a unique morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Spec(R) \longrightarrow Spec(\mathbb{Z})
            %p
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi CRing
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing^{op}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+scheme"} arithmetic scheme
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(R)
              as equipped with a map to the base scheme
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spec%28Z%29"} Spec(Z)
            %p
              Since the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CRing"} CRing
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
              of rings (
              %a{:href => "CRing#CoproductIsTensorProduct"}> prop.
              ), this is the dually the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi CRing
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing^{op}
              and hence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Spec(R \otimes R) \simeq Spec(R) \times Spec(R)
            %p
              exhibits
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \otimes R
              as the ring of functions on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spec
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Spec
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(R) \times Spec(R)
            %p
              Hence the terminal morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(R) \to Spec(\mathbb{Z})
              induces the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+groupoid"} Čech groupoid
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+groupoid"} internal
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi CRing
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing^{op}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Spec
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ×
