          %p
          #NoOtherCharZeroFieldIsSolid.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (no other
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+zero"} characteristic zero
                is a
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solid+ring"} solid ring
              %br/
              The same argument shows that no other
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+zero"} characteristic zero
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is a solid ring, since, being a proper
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superset"} superset
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝕂
                      %mo ⊃
                      %mi ℚ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{K} \supset \mathbb{Q}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝕂
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \mathbb{K}
              for which there are
              %em no
              pairs of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi k
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \cdot k \,=\, q
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
              are not a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solid+ring"} solid ring
            %p
              This is, ultimately, the reason why the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+adjunction"} derived
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PL+de+Rham+complex"} PL de Rham
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction+between+simplicial+sets+and+connective+dgc-algebras"} Quillen adjunction between simplicial sets and connective dgc-algebras
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+adjunction"} idempotent
              only over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = \mathbb{Q}
              (where it models
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rationalization"} rationalization
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
              = succeed ");" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+theorem+of+dg-algebraic+rational+homotopy+theory"} fundamental theorem of dg-algebraic rational homotopy theory
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+homotopy+theory"} real homotopy theory
